  ],
  "description": "Functional mono model of the SPL 9842 with the differential-envelope architecture documented in the factory owner’s manual, diagrams 1–6. Attack compares a fast level follower with a slower attack estimate and Sustain compares a longer decay estimate with the same fast follower. The detector fit uses log RMS tracking times of 2 ms, 64 ms and 160 ms, so each difference follows relative level changes. The time constants, detector components and line stages are estimated. The independent bipolar controls cover ±15 dB Attack and ±24 dB Sustain. A native THAT2180 represents the 6.1 mV/dB control law of the factory THAT2181. The source and load are unbalanced equivalents, the line stage clips near the specified +22.4 dBu output ceiling, and linking, LED metering and relay bypass are omitted.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Attack",
      "Sustain"
    ]
  },
  "name": "SPL Transient Designer 9842 DET Model",
  "outputNode": "out",
  "version": 3,
